                  <tbody>
                    <tr><td class="c-good">Current ex_doc, no explicit pin</td><td>Already inherits Markdown — publish docs.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="c-good">Current ex_doc + explicit pin</td><td>Add “markdown”. Genuinely one line.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="c-warn">Old ex_doc, no explicit pin</td><td>Refresh ex_doc, republish.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="c-crit">Old ex_doc + explicit pin</td><td>Refresh ex_doc <b>and</b> add the formatter. Neither alone is sufficient.</td></tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </figure>

            <p>Section 03 splits the causes into an explicit opt-out and a stale build. A repository that
              commits its lockfile can be both at once, and then neither remedy works alone.
              <b>13 of the 30 (43%)</b> were in that fourth state or carried a further docs-configuration
              incompatibility.</p>

            <p>This does not revise Table 2. That census classifies 283 published packages by download
              volume; this is a 30-repository implementation sample selected for having explicit pins, and
              the two denominators are not interchangeable. What it revises is the <em>unit of work</em>:
              from a one-line pull request to a small dependency-aware maintenance change.</p>

